# Commit messages

- Match the style of existing commit messages
- Use Conventional Commits: `type: description`
- Allowed types: `feat` / `fix` / `refactor` / `style` / `docs` / `test` / `chore`
- Write the description in Japanese as a noun phrase (体言止め)—e.g. 「追加」, not 「追加する」
- Omit the body when the subject line is enough
- When a body is needed, use noun-phrase bullet points (`-`)
- Do not mention incidental changes unrelated to the main change (formatting, reordering, minor comment tweaks, typos, etc.)
